# What never belongs in a build context.
#
# node_modules is the one that matters rather than merely costing time: Dockerfile.web runs
# `npm ci` and then copies web/ over the top, so a host node_modules would overwrite the one just
# installed — with packages built for the host's platform, inside an Alpine image. The failure that
# follows points at a native module and not at this file.

# Dependencies and build output — every one of these is produced inside the image.
**/node_modules
**/bin
**/obj
web/.next
web/out
publish

# Version control and CI. .git alone is tens of megabytes of context that no build step reads.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Credentials. cred.txt holds a Coolify API token; a build context is copied wholesale into the
# daemon and can surface in image layers.
cred.txt
cred*.txt
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Documentation platform and specs — not read by any build stage.
docs
knowledge.md
knowledge.html
*.md
!web/README.md

# Local tooling and editor state.
.vs
.vscode
.idea
.claude
scratchpad
*.user
*.suo
TestResults
